    <item>
      <title>Cost Per Serving Calculator</title>
      <link>https://fedforless.ca/tools/cost-per-serving-calculator/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://fedforless.ca/tools/cost-per-serving-calculator/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Enter what the ingredients you used cost, in total, and how many real servings the recipe made. Real means the portion a hungry adult eats, not the portion that makes the number pretty.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;toolbox nums&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;label for=&#34;cps-total&#34;&gt;Total ingredient cost of the batch ($)&lt;/label&gt;&#xA;  &lt;input id=&#34;cps-total&#34; type=&#34;number&#34; min=&#34;0&#34; step=&#34;0.01&#34; placeholder=&#34;8.02&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;label for=&#34;cps-servings&#34;&gt;Servings the batch actually made&lt;/label&gt;&#xA;  &lt;input id=&#34;cps-servings&#34; type=&#34;number&#34; min=&#34;1&#34; step=&#34;1&#34; placeholder=&#34;6&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;out&#34; id=&#34;cps-out&#34;&gt;Cost per serving: —&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;  &lt;p id=&#34;cps-tier&#34; style=&#34;font-weight:700;color:#2C3138;&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;script&gt;&#xA;(function(){&#xA;  var t=document.getElementById(&#39;cps-total&#39;), s=document.getElementById(&#39;cps-servings&#39;),&#xA;      o=document.getElementById(&#39;cps-out&#39;), tier=document.getElementById(&#39;cps-tier&#39;);&#xA;  function go(){&#xA;    var tv=parseFloat(t.value), sv=parseFloat(s.value);&#xA;    if(tv&gt;=0 &amp;&amp; sv&gt;0){&#xA;      var per=tv/sv;&#xA;      o.textContent=&#39;Cost per serving: $&#39;+per.toFixed(2);&#xA;      tier.textContent = per&lt;=1.50 ? &#39;Fed For Less tier: Tier 1 (up to $1.50).&#39; :&#xA;        per&lt;=2.50 ? &#39;Fed For Less tier: Tier 2 ($1.51 to $2.50).&#39; :&#xA;        per&lt;=3.25 ? &#39;Fed For Less tier: Tier 3 ($2.51 to $3.25), a filling splurge.&#39; :&#xA;        &#39;Above the Fed For Less Tier 3. Worth a cheaper protein or a bigger batch.&#39;;&#xA;    } else { o.textContent=&#39;Cost per serving: —&#39;; tier.textContent=&#39;&#39;; }&#xA;  }&#xA;  t.addEventListener(&#39;input&#39;,go); s.addEventListener(&#39;input&#39;,go);&#xA;})();&#xA;&lt;/script&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;how-to-get-the-batch-cost&#34;&gt;How to get the batch cost&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Price each ingredient by the amount used: the package price divided by the package size, times the amount the recipe takes. Half a bag is half the price. Add a small allowance for spices, oil, salt, and garlic rather than pretending they are free. That total is the batch cost, and the calculator above does the rest.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Recipe Cost Calculator</title>
      <link>https://fedforless.ca/tools/recipe-cost-calculator/</link>
      <pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://fedforless.ca/tools/recipe-cost-calculator/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;This is the exact arithmetic behind every Fed For Less breakdown. For each ingredient, enter the package price, the package size, and the amount your recipe uses, in the same unit (grams with grams, millilitres with millilitres). Add lines as needed.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;toolbox nums&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div id=&#34;rc-lines&#34;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;  &lt;button id=&#34;rc-add&#34; style=&#34;background:var(--denim);color:#fff;border:none;font-weight:800;padding:.7rem 1.2rem;border-radius:6px;cursor:pointer;font:inherit;margin-top:.8rem;&#34;&gt;Add an ingredient line&lt;/button&gt;&#xA;  &lt;label for=&#34;rc-servings&#34;&gt;Servings the recipe makes&lt;/label&gt;&#xA;  &lt;input id=&#34;rc-servings&#34; type=&#34;number&#34; min=&#34;1&#34; step=&#34;1&#34; value=&#34;4&#34;&gt;&#xA;  &lt;div class=&#34;out&#34; id=&#34;rc-out&#34;&gt;Batch total: $0.00 · Per serving: —&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;script&gt;&#xA;(function(){&#xA;  var wrap=document.getElementById(&#39;rc-lines&#39;), out=document.getElementById(&#39;rc-out&#39;),&#xA;      serv=document.getElementById(&#39;rc-servings&#39;);&#xA;  function line(){&#xA;    var d=document.createElement(&#39;div&#39;);&#xA;    d.style.display=&#39;grid&#39;; d.style.gridTemplateColumns=&#39;1fr 1fr 1fr 1fr&#39;; d.style.gap=&#39;.6rem&#39;; d.style.marginTop=&#39;.6rem&#39;;&#xA;    d.innerHTML=&#39;&lt;input type=&#34;number&#34; min=&#34;0&#34; step=&#34;0.01&#34; placeholder=&#34;Pkg price $&#34; class=&#34;rc-p&#34;&gt;&#39;+&#xA;      &#39;&lt;input type=&#34;number&#34; min=&#34;0&#34; step=&#34;any&#34; placeholder=&#34;Pkg size&#34; class=&#34;rc-s&#34;&gt;&#39;+&#xA;      &#39;&lt;input type=&#34;number&#34; min=&#34;0&#34; step=&#34;any&#34; placeholder=&#34;Amount used&#34; class=&#34;rc-u&#34;&gt;&#39;+&#xA;      &#39;&lt;input type=&#34;text&#34; readonly class=&#34;rc-r&#34; placeholder=&#34;$0.00&#34; style=&#34;background:#F2F5F9;&#34;&gt;&#39;;&#xA;    wrap.appendChild(d);&#xA;    d.querySelectorAll(&#39;input&#39;).forEach(function(i){ i.addEventListener(&#39;input&#39;,go); });&#xA;  }&#xA;  function go(){&#xA;    var total=0;&#xA;    wrap.querySelectorAll(&#39;div&#39;).forEach(function(d){&#xA;      var p=parseFloat(d.querySelector(&#39;.rc-p&#39;).value), s=parseFloat(d.querySelector(&#39;.rc-s&#39;).value),&#xA;          u=parseFloat(d.querySelector(&#39;.rc-u&#39;).value), r=d.querySelector(&#39;.rc-r&#39;);&#xA;      if(p&gt;=0 &amp;&amp; s&gt;0 &amp;&amp; u&gt;=0){ var v=p*u/s; r.value=&#39;$&#39;+v.toFixed(2); total+=v; }&#xA;      else r.value=&#39;&#39;;&#xA;    });&#xA;    var sv=parseFloat(serv.value);&#xA;    out.textContent=&#39;Batch total: $&#39;+total.toFixed(2)+&#39; · Per serving: &#39;+(sv&gt;0 ? &#39;$&#39;+(total/sv).toFixed(2) : &#39;—&#39;);&#xA;  }&#xA;  document.getElementById(&#39;rc-add&#39;).addEventListener(&#39;click&#39;,function(){ line(); });&#xA;  serv.addEventListener(&#39;input&#39;,go);&#xA;  line(); line(); line();&#xA;})();&#xA;&lt;/script&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;the-basket-cost-too&#34;&gt;The basket cost, too&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The calculator gives you the cost of what you used. The basket cost is simpler and ruder: add up the full price of every package on the shopping list. A recipe can be gentle per serving and still need a forty dollar basket the first time. Both numbers matter, which is why every recipe here shows both.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
